Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["KPZ at LO: couplings that are functions of p^2", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"8186775a-7d04-4941-a407-987292630770"],

Cell["\<\
The second pipeline of the library (design/LOPIPELINE.md). The Gamma2 \
couplings of KPZ become functions of the momentum: Gamma^(1,1) = i w + nu p^2 \
f_nu(p^2), Gamma^(0,2) = -2 D f_D(p^2), with f_nu(0) = f_D(0) = 1, the vertex \
lambda constant. The library derives the flow of each function at generic p \
(one loop, two pole families: Delta at q and at Q = p + q), the anomalous \
dimensions from f(0) = 1, the dimensionless form at fixed p/k, and writes a \
Python module for BMWflow. The exact comparison with BMWflow's notes \
(LO_flow_equations.tex, kpz_notation.tex) is the benchmark benchmarks/KPZLO; \
this notebook shows the workflow and checks f = 1 against Canet's Eq. (20).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ccd9627-be03-49eb-b118-7d92d492962d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Get[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"95877caa-75ea-49a7-8761-3f7331584fbe"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 InterpretationBox[
  RowBox[{"\<\"FRGscalarMSR \"\>", "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"1.0.0\"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\" -- modules: \"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"Core, Theory, Ansatz, Vertices, Regulator, \
Propagator, Symmetries, Loops, Projection, FrequencyIntegration, Closure, \
Assemble, ExternalMomentum, Oracle, Stages, Dimensions, Adimensional, \
JuliaExport, PythonExport\"\>"}],
  SequenceForm[
  "FRGscalarMSR ", "1.0.0", " -- modules: ", 
   "Core, Theory, Ansatz, Vertices, Regulator, Propagator, Symmetries, Loops, \
Projection, FrequencyIntegration, Closure, Assemble, ExternalMomentum, \
Oracle, Stages, Dimensions, Adimensional, JuliaExport, PythonExport"],
  Editable->False]], "Print",
