Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Ansatz with functions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cb4a5020-b5a8-4da3-83b5-396a00603ff0"],

Cell["\<\
fn[f, X] in the density is f(-Laplacian) acting on X: it multiplies the term \
by f(p^2), p the momentum of X's leg. \"Functions\" -> {f -> reference} \
states f(0) = 1 and names the k-dependent amplitude; the ansatz infers \
\"Pipeline\" -> \"LO\" from the fn. The symmetries take the same tags as in \
DE but no truncation orders: the Galilean Ward identity protects the 1 of i \
w, the shift symmetry h -> h + c makes the p^0 order of Gamma^(1,1) vanish.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"58120e44-7451-4d6f-80aa-b459e327da03"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
theory = DefineTheory[\"Scalars\" -> {h}, \"Dimension\" -> Dim];
ansatz = DefineAnsatz[theory,
  \"Density\" -> hbar (dt[h] - nuk fn[fnu, lap[h]] - lamk/2 grad[h].grad[h]) \
- Dk hbar fn[fD, hbar],
  \"Couplings\" -> {nuk, lamk, Dk}, \"Functions\" -> {fD -> Dk, fnu -> nuk}];\
\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"439ca341-e7ba-427b-b756-773f618d1148"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

