Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. The BMWflow module", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c22ae583-a0d3-4fba-b68c-4b5a2428b94b"],

Cell["\<\
ExportPython writes the module of the contract docs/handoff/BMWflow_LO.md: \
FUNCTIONS, ETAS, COUPLINGS, P2_DIVIDED and the functions linear, loop, \
eta_matrix, eta_vector, beta. The loop measure is not in the kernels (the \
adapter applies it); primes on f are d/d|momentum|. \"G\" -> alamk^2 writes \
every kernel in BMWflow's coupling g = alamk^2 (COUPLINGS = (\"g\",)); \
\"Model\" is a label.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"427c136a-eedc-4fc8-8762-9dcd6efce2f5"],

Cell["\<\
ExportPython[adim, \"G\" -> alamk^2, \"Model\" -> \"KPZ\", \"File\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"KPZLO\", \"KPZ_LO.py\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c68985c7-dc15-4137-a0a9-bfc166a46a85"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
